course: dictionary
lesson: 7485
title: Possession: owning things and having control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A possession is something you own. Possessions are all the things a person owns, such as clothes, toys and books. «Zacchaeus gave half his possessions to the poor» means he gave away some of the things he owned.
explain: In sport, a team has possession when it controls the ball. In football or netball, the team with possession is the team holding or moving the ball. The meaning is about control, not just owning.
explain: Possession also has other meanings. Some phrases use it: «take possession of» means to take control of something, «in possession of» means to have something, and a «prized possession» is something you value very much. The apostrophe is different: in «the dog's bone», it shows that the bone belongs to the dog.
fact: Possession means having or owning something.
fact: Possessions means the things a person owns.
fact: In football and netball, a team has possession when it controls the ball.
fact: «Possession» has two pairs of s's, like two pairs of shoes.
fact: «Possession» is on the National Curriculum list of words that children in Years 3 and 4 should learn to spell.
exercise: «Zacchaeus gave half his possessions to the poor.» What are his possessions? | The trees he climbed | *The things he owned | The friends he had in Jericho | The food he cooked for the poor
exercise: In netball, «the team has possession» means what? | The team has a new coach | The team has lost the game | The team is tired and wants to stop | *The team has control of the ball
exercise: In «the dog's bone», what does the apostrophe show? | *The bone belongs to the dog | The dog is missing | The dog is angry | The bone is broken
test: «She took possession of the old house.» What does took possession of mean? | Gave the house away | Sold the house quickly | Hid in the house | *Took control of the house or became its owner
test: What does a «prized possession» mean? | *Something you value very much | Something you must give back | Something you have stolen | Something that is broken
exam: Which word means the things a person owns? | possessing | possessed | possess | *possessions
